From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: quiet the per-call log now the race is gone

The per-call console lines cost about 120 ms per RPC (median round trip 94 ms
with them, 0.6 ms without) and, until the previous patch, were load-bearing:
they were the accidental settle that kept the ARM from advancing the MIPS's
NewCall read pointer before the BG-thread had read it. That race is fixed at
its source now (the driver no longer touches share_seq + 32), so the lines are
free to go where they belong.

Every per-call line moves to pr_debug: the IPC trace, the TX FreeCall/slot/chan
lines, the doorbell SENT line, the msgbox rx/tx words, and the return-FIFO
lines. dynamic debug brings any of them back by name when a problem needs them.
Verified after the fix with the console muted: 100 back-to-back calls, 0 lost,
median 0.46 ms -- the throughput the logging was hiding.

What stays at pr_info/pr_warn: probe, ready, firmware, reset, the timeout
warning, and everything that fires at most a handful of times a boot. The
counters and the FreeCall ring are in /sys/kernel/debug/cpu_comm/watch, not on
the console.

diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_channel.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_channel.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_channel.c	2026-09-07 17:42:50.564233564 +0200
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_channel.c	2026-09-07 17:43:18.441812094 +0200
@@ -787,7 +787,7 @@
 
 	cur_node = cc_deref(fifo_hdr[14]);	/* head.next */
 
-	pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: GetReturnbySessionId session=0x%x cpu=%u: list head.next=0x%lx sentinel=0x%lx count=%d\n",
+	pr_debug("cpu_comm: GetReturnbySessionId session=0x%x cpu=%u: list head.next=0x%lx sentinel=0x%lx count=%d\n",
 		session_id, cpu, cur_node, sentinel, fifo_hdr[13]);
 
 	while (cur_node && cur_node != sentinel) {
@@ -894,13 +894,13 @@
 	sock = &s_CommSockt[1248 * cpu];
 	sem = &sock[283];			/* MsgFIFO semaphore */
 
-	pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: returnPipeLine cpu=%u: share_seq_r=0x%lx fifo[rd=%u wr=%u peak=%u sem=%u cap=%u itemsz=%u base=0x%x]\n",
+	pr_debug("cpu_comm: returnPipeLine cpu=%u: share_seq_r=0x%lx fifo[rd=%u wr=%u peak=%u sem=%u cap=%u itemsz=%u base=0x%x]\n",
 		cpu, share_seq_r, fifo[0], fifo[1], fifo[2], fifo[3], fifo[4], fifo[5], fifo[6]);
 
 	cpu_comm_sem_down((void *)sem);
 
 	item_addr = fifo_getItemRd(fifo);
-	pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: returnPipeLine first_item_addr=0x%lx\n", item_addr);
+	pr_debug("cpu_comm: returnPipeLine first_item_addr=0x%lx\n", item_addr);
 
 	while (item_addr) {
 		/* Read the entry pointer from the FIFO slot */
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c	2026-09-07 17:42:50.563490858 +0200
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c	2026-09-07 17:43:18.441279550 +0200
@@ -277,7 +277,7 @@
 	while (readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + ep->fifo)) {
 		raw = readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + ep->data);
 
-		pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: msgbox rx raw=0x%08x (%s)\n",
+		pr_debug("cpu_comm: msgbox rx raw=0x%08x (%s)\n",
 				    raw, cpu_comm_msgbox_type_name(raw));
 
 		if (raw > MSG_TYPE_RETURN_ACK)
@@ -1257,7 +1257,7 @@
 	udelay(10);
 	writel(0, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_EN);
 
-	pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
+	pr_debug("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
 			    raw, cpu_comm_msgbox_type_name(raw),
 			    readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO));
 	writel(raw, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_DATA);
@@ -1265,7 +1265,7 @@
 	udelay(10);
 	writel(0, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_EN);
 
-	pr_info_ratelimited("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
+	pr_debug("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
 			    raw, cpu_comm_msgbox_type_name(raw),
 			    readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO));
 }
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_proto.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_proto.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_proto.c	2026-09-07 17:42:50.562973575 +0200
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_proto.c	2026-09-07 17:43:18.440617425 +0200
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 	 * "callbacks suppressed" message confirmed the limiter was hiding
 	 * events. Revert to pr_info_ratelimited once RETURN-path bug is
